## Implementation Guidelines

### Component Design
- Keep game canvas components focused on rendering and delegating to game logic
- Separate game state from UI state
- Use Svelte stores for persistent game data and settings
- Implement responsive design for different device orientations

### Game Engine Integration

```javascript
// lib/game/core/engine.js
export class GameEngine {
  constructor(canvas, options = {}) {
    this.canvas = canvas;
    this.ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    this.lastTime = 0;
    this.accumulator = 0;
    this.timestep = 1000/60; // Target 60 FPS
    this.entities = [];
    this.systems = [];
    this.inputHandler = null;
    this.isRunning = false;
    
    // Configure with options
    Object.assign(this, options);
  }
  
  init() {
    // Initialize game systems
    return this;
  }
  
  start() {
    this.isRunning = true;
    this.lastTime = performance.now();
    requestAnimationFrame(this.loop.bind(this));
    return this;
  }
  
  stop() {
    this.isRunning = false;
    return this;
  }
  
  loop(timestamp) {
    if (!this.isRunning) return;
    
    const deltaTime = timestamp - this.lastTime;
    this.lastTime = timestamp;
    
    // Fixed timestep updates
    this.accumulator += deltaTime;
    while (this.accumulator >= this.timestep) {
      this.update(this.timestep);
      this.accumulator -= this.timestep;
    }
    
    // Render
    this.render(this.accumulator / this.timestep); // Interpolation factor
    
    requestAnimationFrame(this.loop.bind(this));
  }
  
  update(deltaTime) {
    // Update all game systems and entities
    for (const system of this.systems) {
      system.update(deltaTime);
    }
    
    for (const entity of this.entities) {
      entity.update(deltaTime);
    }
  }
  
  render(interpolation) {
    // Clear canvas
    this.ctx.clearRect(0, 0, this.canvas.width, this.canvas.height);
    
    // Render world and entities
    for (const entity of this.entities) {
      entity.render(this.ctx, interpolation);
    }
  }
}
```

### Svelte Component Integration

```svelte
<!-- src/lib/components/game/Canvas.svelte -->
<script>
  import { onMount, onDestroy } from 'svelte';
  import { GameEngine } from '$lib/game/core/engine';
  import { InputHandler } from '$lib/game/core/input';
  import { Player } from '$lib/game/entities/player';
  import { World } from '$lib/game/world/map';
  import { gameState } from '$lib/stores/game-state';
  
  let canvas;
  let engine;
  
  onMount(() => {
    // Set canvas dimensions
    canvas.width = window.innerWidth;
    canvas.height = window.innerHeight;
    
    // Initialize game
    engine = new GameEngine(canvas, { 
      debug: $gameState.debugMode 
    });
    
    // Setup input handler
    const input = new InputHandler(canvas);
    engine.inputHandler = input;
    
    // Create world and player
    const world = new World(engine);
    const player = new Player(engine, input);
    
    engine.entities.push(world, player);
    
    // Start game loop
    engine.init().start();
    
    // Handle resize
    const handleResize = () => {
      canvas.width = window.innerWidth;
      canvas.height = window.innerHeight;
    };
    
    window.addEventListener('resize', handleResize);
    
    return () => {
      window.removeEventListener('resize', handleResize);
      engine.stop();
    };
  });
</script>

<canvas 
  bind:this={canvas} 
  class="game-canvas"
></canvas>

<style>
  .game-canvas {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    touch-action: none; /* Prevent browser handling of touch events */
  }
</style>
```

### Game State Management with Stores

```javascript
// src/lib/stores/game-state.js
import { writable, derived } from 'svelte/store';
import { browser } from '$app/environment';

// Initial state
const defaultState = {
  playerPosition: { x: 0, y: 0 },
  health: 100,
  abilities: {
    dash: false,
    doubleJump: false,
    wallClimb: false,
    chargedAttack: false
  },
  inventory: [],
  gameTime: 0,
  areasDiscovered: [],
  currentArea: 'start',
  debugMode: false
};

// Create a function to persist state
function createGameState() {
  // Try to load state from localStorage if in browser
  const saved = browser ? 
    JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('gameState') || 'null') : 
    null;
  
  const state = writable(saved || defaultState);
  
  // Subscribe to changes and save to localStorage
  if (browser) {
    state.subscribe(value => {
      localStorage.setItem('gameState', JSON.stringify(value));
    });
  }
  
  return {
    ...state,
    reset: () => state.set(defaultState),
    unlockAbility: (ability) => {
      state.update(s => ({
        ...s,
        abilities: {
          ...s.abilities,
          [ability]: true
        }
      }));
    }
  };
}

export const gameState = createGameState();

// Derived stores for specific parts of state
export const playerAbilities = derived(
  gameState,
  $gameState => $gameState.abilities
);

export const playerProgress = derived(
  gameState,
  $gameState => ({
    areasDiscovered: $gameState.areasDiscovered.length,
    abilitiesUnlocked: Object.values($gameState.abilities).filter(Boolean).length,
    gameTimeMinutes: Math.floor($gameState.gameTime / 60)
  })
);
```

## Performance Considerations

### Canvas Optimization
- Use multiple layered canvases for different elements (background, entities, UI)
- Implement texture atlases and sprite batching
- Only draw entities that are visible within the viewport
- Use requestAnimationFrame with a fixed timestep and interpolation

### Asset Loading
- Implement progressive asset loading during gameplay
- Preload essential assets before game start
- Use a loading screen with progress indicator
- Implement asset caching with service workers

### Memory Management
- Properly dispose of unused resources
- Implement object pooling for frequently created/destroyed objects
- Monitor memory usage with performance tools
- Use WeakMaps for temporary object references

## Accessibility Guidelines
- Support keyboard input as alternative to touch
- Implement high contrast mode for visual elements
- Allow customization of control sensitivity
- Provide text alternatives for important visual cues

## Deployment Considerations
- Use proper cache headers for static assets
- Implement versioning for cache busting
- Configure appropriate compression for assets
- Set up PWA manifest and icons 